{
  "challenges": [
    {
      "publicId": "chal_coding_pdp_132",
      "name": "menu-file-schema-drift",
      "type": "mini_coding",
      "title": "Load menu files that change shape",
      "description": "Partner restaurants send menu CSV exports from their POS vendor, and the vendor changes the columns without warning: last night `price` became `unit_price`, moved, and a new `discount_vnd` appeared, and the old positional loader put prices in the wrong column. The editor holds `pipelines/load_menu.py` with its key blocks missing, each marked by a `# [ ]` line; some pieces are wrong on purpose. Fill every line so that columns are matched by name and known aliases, a file missing a required column is refused without changing the table, new columns are added to the table and reported, rows that do not convert are listed with their line, and more than 5% bad rows refuses the file. Run loads a sequence of files on SQLite and prints each result and the table.",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "outcomes": [
        "extract-load"
      ],
      "points": 30,
      "hints": [
        "Feed tonight's file to your loader in your head column by column: which table column receives `unit_price`, which receives `discount_vnd`, and what tells you the file is missing something the table cannot do without?",
        "Look at a dictionary from every accepted name (`CONTRACT` keys plus `aliases`) to its column, `PRAGMA table_info(...)` for the columns a table has, and `ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN`.",
        "A loader for courier shift files with `courier_id` (alias `driver_id`) and `hours` might build `names = {'courier_id': 'courier_id', 'driver_id': 'courier_id', 'hours': 'hours'}`, map `header[i].strip().lower()` through it, refuse the file when `courier_id` is not among the mapped values, and `ALTER TABLE shifts ADD COLUMN \"bonus\" TEXT` when an unknown `bonus` column shows up."
      ],
      "coding": {
        "language": "python",
        "filePath": "pipelines/load_menu.py",
        "executionMode": "stdio",
        "timeLimitMs": 3000,
        "memoryLimitMb": 128,
        "scoringMode": "all_or_nothing",
        "maxAttempts": null
      },
      "tests": [
